\@writefile{lot}{\contentsline {table}{\numberline {3}{\ignorespaces Budget compliance under cost drift (Experiment\nonbreakingspace 3, 50\nonbreakingspace seeds). Each cell shows realised average cost as a multiple of the budget target ($1.00\times $ = perfect). \textbf  {Bold} marks values within $5\%$ of $1.00\times $. $\dagger $\nonbreakingspace Phase\nonbreakingspace 2 constraint non-binding: the price drop reduces all methods' costs below target, regardless of algorithm. ParetoBandit is the only condition that reliably meets the target in Phase\nonbreakingspace 1 and, where the constraint remains binding (tight), in Phase\nonbreakingspace 2.}}{10}{table.caption.28}\protected@file@percent }
\newlabel{tab:budget_compliance}{{3}{10}{Budget compliance under cost drift (Experiment~3, 50~seeds). Each cell shows realised average cost as a multiple of the budget target ($1.00\times $ = perfect). \textbf {Bold} marks values within $5\%$ of $1.00\times $. $\dagger $~Phase~2 constraint non-binding: the price drop reduces all methods' costs below target, regardless of algorithm. ParetoBandit is the only condition that reliably meets the target in Phase~1 and, where the constraint remains binding (tight), in Phase~2}{table.caption.28}{}}
